  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124477,
      "id": "488c9762-554b-5ea6-b414-ce6cbde9bbd1",
      "title": "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 & -9 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $4$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd, $4$th, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -4 & -9 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
